 "meta": {
  "name": "Fog blindness: the ego can see the pedestrian and does not perceive her",
  "description": "A person is standing in the ego's lane. Nothing is in the way \u2014 the geometric line of sight is open from the first tick of the clip and stays open. What the ego lacks is not visibility, it is perception: in dense fog the apparent contrast of her silhouette falls below the camera's floor long before she is close, so the detection channel reports nothing and the brake trigger does not arm. The danger here IS the perception failure. The control template caps-sensor-clear.template.json is byte-identical apart from the weather preset.",
  "createdAt": "2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z",
  "modifiedAt": "2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z",
